      "urpx:hasCoverageClaim": {
        "@id": "sce:cc-tou-d-5-8pm-2026-03-20",
        "@type": "urpx:CoverageClaim",
        "urpx:completenessResult": {
          "@id": "urpx:partial"
        },
        "urpx:selfContained": true,
        "urpx:explainedBy": {
          "@type": "urpx:Evaluation",
          "@id": "sce:cc-tou-d-5-8pm-2026-03-20-evaluation",
          "urpx:evaluationKind": {
            "@id": "urpx:coverageEvaluation"
          },
          "urpx:description": "Two things published for Option 5-8 PM are not represented in this filing. First, the Option 5-8 PM-CPP variant printed on the same Sheet 4: a CPP Event Energy Charge of $0.80000 per kWh, a Summer on-peak non-event energy credit of $(0.15170) per kWh, and a Summer Season Maximum Available Credit of $(0.58794) per kWh, none of them modeled. Second, the two pilot bill discounts in Special Conditions 15 and 16: the San Joaquin Valley Disadvantaged Communities Pilot Bill Protection Discount (20 percent in years 1 through 5, then 10 or 20 percent in years 6 through 10) and the 20 percent Transitional Community Solar Discount. Several Special Conditions are out of scope rather than missing: the twelve-month rate change restriction in Special Condition 7, the Arrearage Management Plan debt forgiveness in Special Condition 10, and the Discontinued TOU Period provisions of Special Condition 14, whose terms expired for all customers on July 31, 2022, govern account administration rather than price. The Deed Restricted Base Services Charge adjustment of $(0.332) per meter per day and the CARE and FERA discount lines are cross-references to separate schedules, each filed as its own modifier in this corpus. Two things Preliminary Statement Part H states are not represented either: how the kWh-per-day allocations bounding Tier 1 of sce:tou-d-5-8pm-2026-03-20-tiers-baseline scale to a billing period, and the Medical Baseline Allocation it adds to them.",
          "urpx:evaluatedOn": "2026-09-21T00:00:00"
        }
      }
    }
  }
